From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ae-automation-bot <ae-automation-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 07:27:29 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 024/159] [ae-patch] Fix the second review round on the Tabler
 icon loader

Review of https://github.com/analyticendeavors/omnigent-ae/pull/57.

- The asset glob asks for ?url&no-inline, so a library build (the embed)
  emits the two JSON files as assets instead of inlining them as data: URLs
  into a chunk the entry imports statically; a retry never adds a query to a
  data: or blob: URL (aeTablerRetryUrl).
- Own-key lookups use Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call, since Safari and
  iOS 15.0 to 15.3 (still in build.target) lack Object.hasOwn.
- The loader's fetch lives in aeTablerAssetFetch.ts, and test-setup.ts mocks
  it with a disk reader (aeTablerAssetFetch.disk.ts), so no suite reaches the
  global fetch for the icon set.
- The loader retries by itself: on the window online event, and for a new
  subscriber after a failure once a backoff (2 s doubling to 30 s) has passed.
  The picker's Try again loads at once.
- useAeTablerIcons is useSyncExternalStore over the loader
  (subscribeAeTablerIcons, aeTablerIconsState); subscribing starts the load.
- Listeners are notified outside the load's promise chain, each in a
  try/catch, so a throwing listener cannot leave the load rejected.
- Tests find node_modules from the test file's own path, not the working
  directory.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
